{{- /*
	init writes what makes the directory a package: the name every declaration of
	api.py is reached by, and the statement of which of them are the package's own.
	It stands as a file of its own rather than being api.py renamed to __init__.py,
	which would spare it entirely. A package whose whole content is its __init__ has
	to be taken apart before it can gain a second module, and this one is expected
	to — the legacy target already ships an asyncio subpackage beside its modules,
	and the flag choosing between a blocking and an awaiting client is written down
	as the next thing to build.

	The names are listed and not starred. A star would lift whatever api.py holds at
	module level, and what it holds includes the dozen-odd names it imported in
	order to declare anything at all: a package exporting pydantic's Field under its
	own name is a package whose user can import the wrong Field and be told nothing.
	The Go target needs no such statement, an identifier there being exported by how
	it is spelled and an import never being re-exported at all. Python's underscore
	answers only the first half of that, which is why the second half is written.

	The surface is stated twice — bound by the import, declared by __all__ — because
	the two are read by different things. The import is what puts a name in the
	package; __all__ is what a star import takes and, more to the point, what a type
	checker reads to decide that a name reached through this module was meant to be.
	Without it a bot checked strictly is told the package exports nothing.

	The transport comes first and in the order api.py declares it, the documented
	declarations after and in the order the page numbers them. Neither list is
	sorted: a name moves here only when it moves there.
*/}}
{{- define "init"}}{{/*gotype: github.com/andreychh/tgen/targets/pythonv2.Generation*/ -}}
{{template "header" .}}

from .api import (
    TELEGRAM_API,
    Call,
    Connection,
    Destination,
    Error,
    FakeConnection,
    HTTPConnection,
    Payload,
    Response,
{{- range .Spec.Definitions}}
    {{.Name}},
{{- end}}
)

__all__ = [
    "TELEGRAM_API",
    "Call",
    "Connection",
    "Destination",
    "Error",
    "FakeConnection",
    "HTTPConnection",
    "Payload",
    "Response",
{{- range .Spec.Definitions}}
    "{{.Name}}",
{{- end}}
]
{{end}}
